{"content":"💡 **SUGGESTION: the re-sent frame's fresh id is never registered — `reasoning_details` keyed by it are silently dropped**

When a re-send merges into an existing block whose id is already set, the frame's new id is never adopted and never entered into `toolCallBlocksById` (see `_applyToolCallIdentity`: only fills when `block.id.isEmpty`). Any `reasoning_details` entry that arrives keyed by the **new** id then misses `toolCallBlocksById`, lands in `pendingReasoningDetailsByToolCallId`, and is never attached to the block — the encrypted thought signature is lost for that call. That degrades multi-turn contexts on relays that pair encrypted reasoning with re-send stutter (Anthropic-style signatures on OpenAI-compat endpoints).

Cheap fix: when merging a re-send into a block with a settled id, still register the alias:

```dart
if (resend != null) {
  final newId = rawToolCall['id'] as String?;
  if (newId != null && newId.isNotEmpty && !toolCallBlocksById.containsKey(newId)) {
    toolCallBlocksById[newId] = block;
  }
}
```

(Apply before `_applyToolCallIdentity`, or fold into it behind a flag.) Minor and edge-case; fine to defer.
